# apps/mobile configuration. Copy to apps/mobile/.env.local (gitignored).
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* is the only prefix Expo inlines into the app bundle, so these
# reach the device.
#
# Metro caches inlined env values. After editing this file, restart with:
#   npm run start --workspace @itera/mobile -- --clear

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime mode: 'demo' (default) or 'cloud'.
#
# You do not need this file at all to run the app. With no configuration the
# build is a DEMO build: it opens the product immediately over a deterministic
# demo workspace, needs no Supabase project, asks for no sign-in code and makes
# no cloud request. That is the current default while the product is being shown
# to potential users.
#
# Demo data is deterministic demo data. It is not synced, not cloud-backed, not
# a persisted account and not production data, and it resets on a full app
# restart by design.
#
# Only the exact value 'cloud' selects cloud mode. Anything else - a typo, a
# blank value, 'production' - is demo, so a half-configured build is never
# mistaken for a cloud build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ITERA_MODE=cloud

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud mode only. Required when EXPO_PUBLIC_ITERA_MODE=cloud; with the mode set
# and these unset, the app renders a configuration notice instead of the product.
# There is no native local storage fallback, and a web workspace that only exists
# in a browser will not appear here.
#
# From your Supabase project: Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys. Use the
# PUBLISHABLE key (sb_publishable_...), which is the value Supabase now shows
# where the docs used to say "anon key". The SECRET key must never appear in a
# mobile build - it bypasses Row Level Security.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
